<BaseLayout title="Axon | Providers | NoRec.US" description="Body-worn and in-car cameras, cloud evidence management, real-time video, ALPR, sensors, and public-safety software." active="surveillance">
<main class="page_shell provider_detail">
  <header class="article_header provider_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">PROVIDER / PLATFORM</p>
    <h1>Axon</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">Body-worn and in-car cameras, cloud evidence management, real-time video, ALPR, sensors, and public-safety software.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="provider_scope_notice">
    <span class="status_label">EVIDENCE SCOPE</span>
    <p><strong>Vendor capability</strong> describes the provider’s published product features. <strong>Illinois deployment</strong> is listed only when supported by Illinois records or a clearly labeled secondary source.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">ILLINOIS CONNECTION</p>
    <h2>Documented Illinois relationships</h2>
    <div class="provider_evidence_grid">
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Secretary of State Police</h3><p>Illinois procurement records identify Axon body-worn camera equipment/software for Secretary of State Police.</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>McHenry County</h3><p>County documentation describes a body/in-car video equipment package stored in Evidence.com, tying the local evidence workflow to Axon's platform.</p></article>
      <article><span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span><h3>Huntley</h3><p>Public surveillance documentation identifies Axon body-worn cameras in Huntley.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRODUCT / PLATFORM CAPABILITY</p>
    <h2>Published product capabilities</h2>
    <div class="provider_capability_grid">
      <article><h3>Axon Body 4</h3><p>Axon describes Body 4 as a connected body-worn camera with a 160-degree field of view, livestreaming/geolocation capabilities, and integration with Axon Evidence.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Axon Evidence</h3><p>Axon's cloud evidence system stores and manages video, audio, images, documents, metadata, audit trails, sharing, retention and redaction workflows.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Fleet / vehicle systems</h3><p>Axon's current catalog includes Fleet in-car systems, and newer products such as Outpost and Lightpost also advertise ALPR and vehicle-attribute recognition.</p></article>
      <article><h3>AI-enabled evidence tools</h3><p>Axon markets transcription, redaction, report drafting, search, and other AI-assisted evidence workflows. These capabilities are not attributed to an Illinois customer without a contract or configuration record.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY / GOVERNANCE QUESTIONS</p>
    <h2>Privacy and governance</h2>
    <div class="provider_questions">
      <details><summary>Evidence retention</summary><p>Axon Evidence supports organization-specific retention settings and displays effective retention/deletion status per evidence item.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Auditability</summary><p>Axon says actions on evidence are recorded and that evidence has audit trails and file-integrity validation.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Location metadata</summary><p>Axon Evidence can display GPS coordinates/timestamps/movement paths when such metadata is available.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Platform breadth</summary><p>The Axon catalog extends beyond body cameras. Vendor capability is kept separate from features shown by records to be purchased or enabled by an Illinois agency.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>


